://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nAdd a read-API journey over records written by onepipeline 0.96.0 for a private GitHub Projects plan home with a public-repository task. It covers node states, merged settlement rendering, timeline events, and a missing-run response.\n\nKeep the engine and store versions already adopted by the default branch, and document their private-board support and matching Rust-version declaration.\n\n## Why\n\nHosts need the read API to match the engine dispatching their runs so they can adopt private GitHub boards for mixed plans while the browser view and supervising routes continue reading those runs correctly.\n\n## Additional info\n\nThe engine upgrade and its Rust API break are already present on the default branch; this change adds compatibility coverage without changing the HTTP contract or Rust 1.97 minimum. The fixtures retain engine-written records, with their provenance and regeneration instructions documented alongside them.","created_at":"2026-10-30T05:25:08Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T06:49:19Z","closed_at":"2026-10-30T06:49:17Z","merged_at":"2026-10-30T06:49:17Z","merge_commit_sha":"0dd20868e05cacfc44c398c0b014fa986385ca45","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pulls/546/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pulls/546/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.git