/avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nRelink the read API from `onepipeline` 0.44.2 to exactly **0.45.0** and from `onemessagebus` 0.8.0 to **0.9.0**, with matching sibling releases. The dependency graph now contains one engine, one bus core, and no `onemessagebus-agent`; a packaging test enforces this. Filter-grammar checks now follow onepipeline's types and its `agent.event-filter@1` schema.\n\n**The engine upgrade changed no served shapes.** Existing payload fixtures remain unchanged; `/healthz` reports `onepipeline_version: \"0.45.0\"` in its existing shape.\n\n## Why\n\nThe bus is becoming generic: protocols and vocabulary belong to the libraries that own them. This removes the read API's dependency on the retired agent crate while preserving existing wire formats, and lets the host align its reader and engine versions.\n\n## Additional info\n\n**Breaking Rust API dependency change:** public methods expose onepipeline types, so the engine's 0.44 → 0.45 move changes their type identity. The commit announces this with `feat(deps)!`, as required by the repository's semver guard.\n\nRecorded validation on `f11f511`:\n\n- With an isolated `ONEHARNESS_HISTORY_DIR`, `just test` passed all 438 crate tests, with 15 baseline/cost tests skipped by design and 95.78% line coverage. This includes real-server contract journeys, unchanged byte-for-byte payload fixtures, and comparisons with the 0.45.0 CLI's `telemetry`, `results`, `goals`, `transcript`, and `unwatched` output. Frontend unit tiers passed. Two Playwright journeys failed under reported host load—the supervise-adopt journey and graph-row drill—and both passed in isolated reruns (`2 passed`); the combined browser run was not wholly green.\n- `just lint-llm-diff origin/main`: 52 rules, 12 passed, 0 failed, 29 skipped, 11 not relevant.\n- Both new guards were exercised with deliberate failures, then restored: an extra `round` matcher field failed the schema comparison, and the pre-upgrade lockfile failed the retired-agent dependency assertion.\n\nAn earlier `just test`, before the packaging test and maintainer-note additions, passed 435/437 crate tests. The harness-adoption journey encountered contention on the shared history index lock; it and its failure-path sibling passed with private history storage, with the adoption journey completing in 0.9 seconds. The judge-decision route journey timed out reading a socket and passed in isolation. The shared-history isolation gap was filed as a follow-up.\n\n### Previous gate refusal (CI run 36073002952)\n\nThe first publication of this same tree failed the `gate` job on one Playwright journey: `falls back to the empty state once no run is left` (`apps/dag-ui-e2e/dag-ui.spec.ts:4405`). \"No DAG runs found\" did not appear within the 15s expect budget; the other 132 of 133 journeys passed. **The cause is unidentified.** The run kept no artifact, and the log records no timing to read it from. The tree is republished unchanged, on the manager's ruling. The evidence that the engine move did not cause it:\n\n- Local timing from the final run removal to the empty state, with the same bundle and journeys, against a server built from `main` (engine 0.44.2) and from this branch (0.45.0). With a CI-like PATH (no `claude`/`codex`): 0.36s on main, 0.24s on the branch. With this host's full PATH: ~10s on both, because each status read spawns the harness CLIs (filed as a separate follow-up). CI has neither binary, so this is not the CI cause.\n- The engine source diff 0.44.2 → 0.45.0 touches nothing in run listing or watching, `src/store.rs` removal detection is unchanged, and `oneharness` did not move in the lock.\n- This journey did not fail in the earlier failed gate runs that were checked (35845738470, 35619406022, 35582165213).\n- It passed on this branch in a full local e2e run and in three isolated runs of it with its predecessor journey. That full run failed two other timeline-click journeys under host load average ~73; they are timing-sensitive span overlaps unrelated to this diff.\n","created_at":"2026-09-24T23:29:42Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T14:17:59Z","closed_at":"2026-10-29T14:17:59Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pulls/105/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pulls/105/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/issues/105/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/statuses/f11f5110fe0d7229ace89db918abf5f53877624f","head":{"label":"nickderobertis:onevcs/s-fb12f9450c27","ref":"onevcs/s-fb12f9450c27","sha":"f11f5110fe0d7229ace89db918abf5f53877624f","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gr