chived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":73,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":0,"open_issues":73,"watchers":1,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pulls/446"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pull/446"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/issues/446"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/issues/446/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pulls/446/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pulls/446/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/statuses/e2af4ca98886b689292725b81a8651ed880c19a4"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pulls/444","id":4983925225,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTx3Fc88AAAABKRCp6Q","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pull/444","diff_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pull/444.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pull/444.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/issues/444","number":444,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"perf: keep the Observatory current from pushed changes instead of refetching","user":{"login":"nickderobertis","id":19440155,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDQwMTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nReplace browser polling and full-payload refetches with resumable pushed changes for the sidebar and visible Graph, Overall, node timeline or Channel view. Hidden views stop subscribing, and the run header’s activity line updates live. The server uses incremental engine reads and gzip with per-frame flushing.\n\nAdd dedicated load telemetry and five budgets covering requests, wire traffic, display lag and server CPU. Ensure quiet graphs fit their canvas on opening, and isolate installation builds so they cannot interfere with concurrently running CLI tests.\n\n## Why\n\nThe Observatory stays open for hours on shared hosts. Re-reading whole journals and payloads made even finished-run pages generate hundreds of requests per minute, while live views consumed substantial bandwidth and server CPU. Sending only visible changes keeps those pages quiet and responsive; the budgets guard against regressions.\n\n## Additional info\n\nSchema 25 documents the subscription protocol and adds `run.live_activity`. Healthy subscription streams send patches without repeating snapshots; reconnects replay retained changes, with an explicit reset when resuming is no longer possible. The legacy event stream remains available to existing API consumers. The engine dependency moves to 0.87.1, changing engine types exposed through the crate’s public API; see [engine dependency history](docs/engine-dependency-history.md).\n\n[Committed load telemetry](apps/dag-ui-e2e/telemetry/request-load.json) now comes from a full load run on clean commit `ef9d1d0`, linking engine 0.87.1, and supersedes the earlier measurements at `8821e12`. It records zero observation-window requests per minute on settled, stopped and live run pages, worst single-tab wire traffic of 0.162 MB/min, worst single-tab append-to-display lag p95 of 2.355 seconds, and maximum server CPU of 0.4299 cores per live tab—all within the five budget thresholds. The two-tab variants reach a worst display-lag p95 of 2.182 seconds. Measurements use 150 runs across 30 projects, a 116,000-record live journal, 120-second observation windows, and fresh servers and corpora for each variant. The only subsequent commit records that telemetry.","created_at":"2026-10-23T14:01:01Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T20:48:17Z","closed_at":"2026-10-23T20:48:15Z","merged_at":"2026-10-23T20:48:15Z","merge_commit_sha":"4570176435f743c56b42423bb35ab1086ed1daca","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pulls/444/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pulls/444/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/issues/444/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onepipeline-ui/statuses/ec9c9ce52d58e0344426727bd2790d1fd7ced15c","head":{"label":"nickderobertis:nic