s://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19440155?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nLink `onepipeline` 0.79.0 with `onetaskgraph-*` 0.8.0 and `onevcs` 0.56.3 so browser-adopted runs project landing closures onto board cards. Add adoption journeys for completed-task reconciliation and a real landing carrying `Closes #7`, plus checks enforcing the linked store’s identity.\n\n## Why\n\nThe read API drives adopted runs with its own engine. Keeping it aligned with the dispatching engine lets adopted runs move the cards their landings close and reconcile completed follow-ups instead of leaving them looking open.\n\n## Additional info\n\nBreaking Rust API identity change: the engine upgrade changes the `onepipeline::Error` type accepted by `ApiError::from_engine` and other engine-typed public items. Browser rendering, routes and open-item response shapes remain unchanged; status handling stays in the linked store.","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:33:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T02:03:06Z","closed_at":"2026-10-20T02:03:04Z","merged_at":"2026-10-20T02:03:04Z","merge_commit_sha":"65c7c3f5f12f2a376fd70edf4c4e35fc1eef1291","assignees":[],"requeste